From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wmvcore: Reset the async reader start state on close.

0009-fix-for-arcania-games-video-playback skips a Start() whose range
matches the active one while clock_start is set. Only Stop() cleared
clock_start: a reader closed while it was started kept it, and the first
Start() after reopening was ignored as a duplicate ("Ignoring duplicate
start for active range 0.0"), so the reader never read or delivered a
sample.

Angel Wish (#982) closes its WMA readers without stopping them when the
Windows version is Windows 10 (on Windows 2000 it stops them first). After
the first reopen no audio was delivered and the game hung at the logos.

Clear clock_start and the active range in async_reader_close(), after the
callback thread has exited.
---
--- a/dlls/wmvcore/async_reader.c
+++ b/dlls/wmvcore/async_reader.c
@@ -848,6 +848,12 @@
     reader->streams = NULL;
     reader->stream_count = 0;
 
+    /* Only Stop() cleared this. A reader closed while started kept it, and
+     * Start() after reopening was then skipped as a duplicate. */
+    reader->clock_start = 0;
+    reader->active_start = 0;
+    reader->active_duration = 0;
+
     if (reader->allocator)
         IWMReaderAllocatorEx_Release(reader->allocator);
     reader->allocator = NULL;
